542
00:31:37,133 --> 00:31:38,178
Excuse me.

543
00:31:38,352 --> 00:31:40,702
[scrapes loudly]

544
00:31:45,185 --> 00:31:47,056
What are we drinking?

545
00:31:48,188 --> 00:31:50,320
A 1979 Chateau Lafayette.

546
00:31:50,494 --> 00:31:51,931
- Mm.
- Wine and furniture

547
00:31:52,105 --> 00:31:55,064
are the only two things
the French do well.

548
00:31:55,238 --> 00:31:58,589
- Oh, I don't know--
- But they do them very well.

549
00:31:59,634 --> 00:32:03,203
It's all sauces
to hide the rotting meat.

550
00:32:03,377 --> 00:32:04,856
Their food...

551
00:32:05,727 --> 00:32:07,729
...is like their women.

552
00:32:09,078 --> 00:32:11,080
They all stink without perfume.

553
00:32:11,254 --> 00:32:13,822
Yeah, well,
maybe if they'd have killed

554
00:32:14,083 --> 00:32:15,824
20 million men in 50 years
like you guys,

555
00:32:16,085 --> 00:32:18,131
they could have improved
their herd's aroma, huh?

556
00:32:18,392 --> 00:32:20,524
They didn't have
20 million to spare.

557
00:32:26,226 --> 00:32:28,315
There's a line, Byron,

558
00:32:28,576 --> 00:32:30,012
and you crossed it.

559
00:32:30,926 --> 00:32:32,580
And now there is no line.

560
00:32:33,363 --> 00:32:35,409
Oh, well, you are on
the wrong side of the Atlantic

561
00:32:35,583 --> 00:32:37,237
to be making the rules.

562
00:32:37,411 --> 00:32:38,673
We make the rules here.

563
00:32:38,934 --> 00:32:40,544
And for you,
we're making new ones.

564
00:32:40,805 --> 00:32:43,069
We know what you took...

565
00:32:43,895 --> 00:32:45,767
...we know who took it

566
00:32:45,941 --> 00:32:47,334
and who took it with her.

567
00:32:47,595 --> 00:32:49,727
♪ tense, dramatic music ♪

568
00:32:50,598 --> 00:32:51,686
[clears throat]

569
00:32:51,860 --> 00:32:53,383
You're not down two.

570
00:32:53,557 --> 00:32:54,819
You're down five.

571
00:32:55,037 --> 00:32:56,560
And the two
that are still breathing,

572
00:32:56,734 --> 00:32:58,040
they're en route to somewhere

573
00:32:58,301 --> 00:32:59,737
where no one is going
to hear them scream

574
00:32:59,999 --> 00:33:02,392
when they don't answer
the questions that we ask.

575
00:33:02,566 --> 00:33:04,046
You have no intel.

576
00:33:04,307 --> 00:33:05,830
You have no surveillance.

577
00:33:06,092 --> 00:33:08,572
What you need to do now
is decide who from your embassy

578
00:33:08,746 --> 00:33:10,531
that we're deporting tomorrow,

579
00:33:10,792 --> 00:33:13,229
because I will clean
your fucking office out.

580
00:33:13,490 --> 00:33:14,709
Do you understand me?

581
00:33:15,579 --> 00:33:19,061
You have no play except
to sit here and suck on it.

582
00:33:19,888 --> 00:33:21,324
Or...

583
00:33:21,629 --> 00:33:23,022
you can pull your troops
out of Eastern Ukraine.

584
00:33:23,196 --> 00:33:25,328
- Ah.
- Better for you, right?

585
00:33:25,589 --> 00:33:26,677
Blame everything on us,

586
00:33:26,938 --> 00:33:28,201
wipe some of that egg
off your face

587
00:33:28,462 --> 00:33:29,289
from the ass-whupping
you've been taking

588
00:33:29,463 --> 00:33:31,073
for the last few years?

589
00:33:31,247 --> 00:33:32,596
What do you want?

590
00:33:32,770 --> 00:33:34,033
Want?

591
00:33:34,294 --> 00:33:35,469
To trade?

592
00:33:37,558 --> 00:33:38,863
Oh, gee. Um...

593
00:33:39,038 --> 00:33:40,691
I don't know.
I mean, you already gave us

594
00:33:40,865 --> 00:33:42,824
our weed-vaping
basketball player back.

595
00:33:42,998 --> 00:33:44,260
I'd say we're pretty good.

596
00:33:44,521 --> 00:33:46,480
- We have your marine.
- Mm-hmm. Yes, you do.

597
00:33:46,654 --> 00:33:47,655
Journalist?

598
00:33:47,829 --> 00:33:49,787
One of those two, yeah.

599
00:33:49,961 --> 00:33:51,876
Iran has one as well.

600
00:33:52,138 --> 00:33:53,226
I'm aware.

601
00:33:53,530 --> 00:33:55,793
So, I think we can
work something out.

602
00:33:55,967 --> 00:33:58,231
No. Not looking
for a trade, Maxim.

603
00:33:58,492 --> 00:34:00,711
Then why are you sitting
at my table?

604
00:34:00,972 --> 00:34:03,018
Because you targeted
a State Department official

605
00:34:03,192 --> 00:34:04,976
on U.S. soil, you motherfucker.

606
00:34:05,151 --> 00:34:09,068
You're about to learn
how long our fingers are.

607
00:34:14,986 --> 00:34:17,119
All this shit
tastes the same to me.

608
00:34:17,380 --> 00:34:20,209
You're not a connoisseur, Maxim.
You're a sucker.

609
00:34:21,906 --> 00:34:23,821
You don't have him.

610
00:34:23,995 --> 00:34:26,607
I don't have one. I have two.

611
00:34:26,868 --> 00:34:30,001
That we pulled off a roof
in fucking Fairfax.

612
00:34:30,785 --> 00:34:32,003
And there is not
a goddamn thing in the world

613
00:34:32,178 --> 00:34:33,353
that I'd trade for 'em.

614
00:34:33,570 --> 00:34:35,616
And once we have wrung
every ounce

615
00:34:35,790 --> 00:34:37,748
of information out of them,

616
00:34:38,009 --> 00:34:40,447
we're gonna feed him
to the feral hogs at Gitmo.

617
00:34:41,274 --> 00:34:42,971
I'll send you some bacon.

618
00:34:43,232 --> 00:34:45,365
And that's a fucking promise.

619
00:34:45,626 --> 00:34:47,497
You know what? I'm gonna
make you another promise.

620
00:34:47,671 --> 00:34:49,020
You tried to touch us here?

621
00:34:49,195 --> 00:34:50,631
[scoffs]

622
00:34:52,023 --> 00:34:53,503
It's a two-way street, buddy.

623
00:34:53,677 --> 00:34:55,114
[chair scrapes]

624
00:34:56,811 --> 00:34:58,987
♪

625
00:35:04,035 --> 00:35:06,037
♪ fast, suspenseful music ♪

626
00:35:06,212 --> 00:35:08,127
[faint radio chatter]

627
00:35:25,666 --> 00:35:28,408
♪

628
00:35:28,582 --> 00:35:30,584
[engine starts]

629
00:35:30,758 --> 00:35:32,107
[vehicle door closes]

630
00:35:42,552 --> 00:35:44,815
♪

631
00:36:03,573 --> 00:36:05,575
- Hey. Hey.
- Hmm?

632
00:36:05,836 --> 00:36:07,882
- Hang in there.
- Yeah, yeah.

633
00:36:08,056 --> 00:36:09,927
Debrief...

634
00:36:10,101 --> 00:36:12,278
and you're home.

635
00:36:13,104 --> 00:36:15,368
- Where's home?
- Camp Peary.

636
00:36:16,151 --> 00:36:17,805
Your family's en route.

637
00:36:18,719 --> 00:36:20,677
It's, uh... it's a nice house.

638
00:36:24,246 --> 00:36:26,030
Last resident was a four-star.

639
00:36:26,292 --> 00:36:28,163
You know how those guys
like to live.

640
00:36:29,730 --> 00:36:30,557
On base?

641
00:36:30,818 --> 00:36:32,994
- Yeah.
- [door opens]

642
00:36:35,214 --> 00:36:37,041
Oh, shit.

643
00:36:37,955 --> 00:36:38,956
Evening, sir.

644
00:36:39,130 --> 00:36:41,220
Goddamn it.

645
00:36:42,351 --> 00:36:45,702
When I write my memoirs,

646
00:36:45,876 --> 00:36:48,836
my lack of sleep is gonna
dominate the narrative.

647
00:36:49,010 --> 00:36:50,403
[Meade chuckles]

648
00:36:50,664 --> 00:36:52,492
[Mullins]
Family okay, Joe?

649
00:36:54,581 --> 00:36:55,930
Yes, sir.

650
00:36:59,629 --> 00:37:00,935
You okay?

651
00:37:02,806 --> 00:37:04,155
Well...

652
00:37:04,417 --> 00:37:08,638
my definition of "okay"
keeps changing, sir.

653
00:37:09,857 --> 00:37:11,554
It comes with the job.

654
00:37:13,991 --> 00:37:18,996
Someday,
you're gonna move to a desk.

655
00:37:19,170 --> 00:37:21,738
Station chief, maybe.

656
00:37:22,652 --> 00:37:25,655
It's time.

657
00:37:25,829 --> 00:37:29,006
Then all of these obstacles
and shit that you've overcome

658
00:37:29,180 --> 00:37:32,096
will be the reason
people don't argue

659
00:37:32,358 --> 00:37:33,924
with your recommendations...

660
00:37:34,969 --> 00:37:38,668
...because your understanding
of the consequences

661
00:37:38,929 --> 00:37:40,583
is not theoretical.

662
00:37:43,543 --> 00:37:44,370
No.

663
00:37:44,544 --> 00:37:46,850
- Mm.
- It is not, sir.

664
00:37:47,721 --> 00:37:49,462
Now, let's talk about
the future later.

665
00:37:49,723 --> 00:37:51,725
Right now,
let's talk about your present.

666
00:37:51,899 --> 00:37:53,422
♪ slow, dark music ♪

667
00:37:54,989 --> 00:37:56,599
How was she made?

668
00:37:57,731 --> 00:37:58,906
We don't know.

669
00:37:59,776 --> 00:38:02,518
Most likely a double in Ukraine.

670
00:38:02,779 --> 00:38:04,259
If they knew why she was there,
the attempt

671
00:38:04,433 --> 00:38:05,826
would have been far
more sophisticated.

672
00:38:06,087 --> 00:38:07,958
They sent low-level
Belarus contract agents

673
00:38:08,219 --> 00:38:10,352
that they didn't care
about losing.

674
00:38:11,135 --> 00:38:14,878
It was, um, it was a probe
more than anything else.

675
00:38:15,139 --> 00:38:17,228
They knew she was in-country,
they know

676
00:38:17,403 --> 00:38:18,839
Yurimov has been taken,

677
00:38:19,143 --> 00:38:21,363
but I don't think
that they've connected the two.

678
00:38:21,537 --> 00:38:23,365
Well, they knew something,
otherwise they wouldn't have

679
00:38:23,626 --> 00:38:26,586
- knocked on her front door.
- No, they wouldn't have.

680
00:38:26,760 --> 00:38:29,023
They would have taken her

681
00:38:29,197 --> 00:38:30,633
like we took him.

682
00:38:30,807 --> 00:38:32,983
Do they think she's involved
in the operation?

683
00:38:33,157 --> 00:38:34,420
I'm sure.

684
00:38:34,594 --> 00:38:36,030
Do they think
he's in our possession?

685
00:38:36,204 --> 00:38:37,901
No, because if they did,

686
00:38:38,162 --> 00:38:40,861
I mean, their reaction would
have been very, very different.

687
00:38:41,122 --> 00:38:42,384
[knock at door]

688
00:38:43,951 --> 00:38:44,908
Is there coffee?

689
00:38:45,082 --> 00:38:46,736
[Meade]
There is.

690
00:38:48,129 --> 00:38:49,696
[liquid pouring]

691
00:38:49,957 --> 00:38:51,872
I was on my fourth glass
of champagne,

692
00:38:52,133 --> 00:38:53,961
so I am going
to need information

693
00:38:54,135 --> 00:38:56,442
delivered in very brief,

694
00:38:56,616 --> 00:38:58,400
very precise phrases.

695
00:38:58,574 --> 00:39:02,099
- Duly noted.
- [knock at door]

696
00:39:07,191 --> 00:39:08,889
You up to speed, ma'am?

697
00:39:10,281 --> 00:39:13,372
I read the action report
on the way over.

698
00:39:13,633 --> 00:39:15,025
Assuming nothing else
has happened...

699
00:39:15,286 --> 00:39:16,679
Byron?

700
00:39:16,940 --> 00:39:18,115
Sir.

701
00:39:18,464 --> 00:39:20,596
You want to give us
a timeline to present?

702
00:39:20,770 --> 00:39:22,076
Sure. Um...

703
00:39:22,337 --> 00:39:24,731
March 4,
a Ukrainian double agent

704
00:39:24,992 --> 00:39:27,124
made contact
with a senior case officer

705
00:39:27,386 --> 00:39:30,737
with information on the location
of Aleksi Yurimov.

706
00:39:30,998 --> 00:39:34,088
Joe was given the assignment,
alongside that case officer,

707
00:39:34,349 --> 00:39:37,308
to apprehend Yurimov, which
we achieved Friday, March 14.

708
00:39:37,483 --> 00:39:40,747
Yurimov is currently being held
at our facility in Jordan

709
00:39:41,008 --> 00:39:42,444
and awaiting transport to Gitmo.

710
00:39:42,705 --> 00:39:44,794
And, depending on
POTUS's position,

711
00:39:45,055 --> 00:39:46,187
either held there indefinitely

712
00:39:46,448 --> 00:39:47,754
or transferred back here
to stand trial

713
00:39:47,928 --> 00:39:49,016
for war crimes against humanity.

714
00:39:49,190 --> 00:39:50,452
[Mason]
Doesn't that require

715
00:39:50,713 --> 00:39:52,323
a U.N. tribunal?

716
00:39:53,020 --> 00:39:55,457
No. We can take the position

717
00:39:55,718 --> 00:39:57,546
that since we have
American citizens

718
00:39:57,720 --> 00:40:00,506
serving observe-and-advise
functions in Ukraine,

719
00:40:00,680 --> 00:40:02,203
that those crimes
are punishable here

720
00:40:02,377 --> 00:40:05,075
because our citizens
are subject to those crimes.

721
00:40:05,249 --> 00:40:07,469
You know, we can also prosecute
for the Wagner Group attacks

722
00:40:07,643 --> 00:40:09,253
against our forces in Syria.

723
00:40:09,515 --> 00:40:11,038
We good?

724
00:40:11,865 --> 00:40:13,344
May I proceed?

725
00:40:13,519 --> 00:40:15,390
By all means.

726
00:40:15,564 --> 00:40:17,305
Upon returning home,
Joe was approached

727
00:40:17,566 --> 00:40:21,222
at her residence by two Belarus
contract agents for Russian SSD.

728
00:40:21,396 --> 00:40:25,705
They attempted to force entry.
Joe neutralized both threats.

729
00:40:25,879 --> 00:40:28,272
Her SRT unit found
an observation team

730
00:40:28,534 --> 00:40:29,535
at the incident site.

731
00:40:29,709 --> 00:40:31,014
They neutralized one.

732
00:40:31,232 --> 00:40:32,755
We're holding the other two
at Langley.

733
00:40:32,929 --> 00:40:36,542
Observation team.
Belarus agents as well?

734
00:40:36,716 --> 00:40:37,978
One American citizen,

735
00:40:38,152 --> 00:40:40,023
two Russian nationals
with green cards.

736
00:40:40,197 --> 00:40:43,723
Assuming the American citizen
is from Russia as well?

737
00:40:43,897 --> 00:40:45,376
[Westfield]
Born in Russia,

738
00:40:45,638 --> 00:40:49,250
moved here in '07, uh,
gained U.S. citizenship in 2016.

739
00:40:49,424 --> 00:40:50,512
Okay, so, sleepers.

740
00:40:50,860 --> 00:40:52,340
- Correct.
- [Mullins] But do we have

741
00:40:52,514 --> 00:40:57,258
any idea how Joe was ID'd?

742
00:40:57,432 --> 00:40:58,868
We have assumptions.

743
00:40:59,086 --> 00:41:01,218
Uh, their presence at Boryspil
is likely extensive,

744
00:41:01,392 --> 00:41:03,743
be it paid informants
who work at the airport

745
00:41:03,917 --> 00:41:06,223
or even
the Ukrainian military itself.

746
00:41:07,311 --> 00:41:08,487
But though brief,

747
00:41:08,748 --> 00:41:10,576
moving from plane to vehicle

748
00:41:10,750 --> 00:41:13,013
at Boryspil
is the likeliest place

749
00:41:13,274 --> 00:41:14,754
that Russian intelligence
could get a visual.

750
00:41:15,015 --> 00:41:17,234
It would seem far more likely
that they identified her

751
00:41:17,408 --> 00:41:19,367
- during the operation, to me.
- [Joe] No one on that side

752
00:41:19,628 --> 00:41:23,110
survived the operation
to identify me, sir.

753
00:41:23,284 --> 00:41:26,374
What about video surveillance?
Satellite imagery?

754
00:41:26,548 --> 00:41:29,072
I was wearing a helmet, glasses.

755
00:41:29,246 --> 00:41:32,380
Those items make
visual referencing impossible.

756
00:41:32,641 --> 00:41:34,600
[Westfield] We don't believe
that she was compromised

757
00:41:34,774 --> 00:41:36,950
at the FOB outside of Pokrovsk.

758
00:41:37,124 --> 00:41:39,822
Likewise, we don't believe
that they have any knowledge

759
00:41:39,996 --> 00:41:41,607
of our direct involvement
in the operation.

760
00:41:41,781 --> 00:41:43,434
If so, they would have
aggressively sought out

761
00:41:43,609 --> 00:41:45,393
our exfil, they'd have
neutralized the base.

762
00:41:45,654 --> 00:41:48,701
Their... their reaction would
have been completely different.

763
00:41:48,875 --> 00:41:51,268
As it were, it is likely

764
00:41:51,442 --> 00:41:52,705
that they were aware
of the capture

765
00:41:52,966 --> 00:41:54,097
until after Joe was stateside.

766
00:41:54,358 --> 00:41:55,621
Or en route, anyway.

767
00:41:55,795 --> 00:41:56,796
[Mason]
So, a fluke.

768
00:41:56,970 --> 00:41:58,232
Video surveillance picks her up

769
00:41:58,493 --> 00:42:00,974
at the airport
and A.I. cross-references

770
00:42:01,148 --> 00:42:03,280
- a library of images.
- Correct.

771
00:42:03,542 --> 00:42:05,152
I mean, they have
incomplete data hauls

772
00:42:05,326 --> 00:42:07,763
from the Shadow Brokers
attack in '17.

773
00:42:08,024 --> 00:42:09,809
The SolarWinds attack in 2020.

774
00:42:09,983 --> 00:42:11,419
They had her picture,

775
00:42:11,637 --> 00:42:13,203
they had her listing
as a State Department official

776
00:42:13,377 --> 00:42:15,423
and now an image
placing her in Ukraine.

777
00:42:15,684 --> 00:42:17,599
Look, if they knew that
she was Special Activities,

778
00:42:17,860 --> 00:42:19,993
they'd have never knocked
on that front door.

779
00:42:20,820 --> 00:42:21,821
May I speak?

780
00:42:21,995 --> 00:42:23,126
Go ahead, Joe.

781
00:42:23,300 --> 00:42:26,042
I've been everywhere, doing...

782
00:42:26,303 --> 00:42:27,566
[chuckles]

783
00:42:27,827 --> 00:42:29,263
[sighs]

784
00:42:29,524 --> 00:42:31,439
They've had ample opportunity
to make me,

785
00:42:31,613 --> 00:42:33,310
and they never have.

786
00:42:34,442 --> 00:42:36,531
Then we meet
a Ukrainian double agent

787
00:42:36,705 --> 00:42:40,100
who, unsolicited,
offers us a giant prize.

788
00:42:40,361 --> 00:42:42,276
Two weeks later,
we have the prize,

789
00:42:42,537 --> 00:42:45,801
and now you have contract agents
and SSD knocking on doors

790
00:42:46,062 --> 00:42:49,718
and climbing rooftops
in some neighborhood in Fairfax.

791
00:42:49,892 --> 00:42:52,112
Occam's razor theorizes
that the solution

792
00:42:52,373 --> 00:42:53,679
with the least amount
of variables

793
00:42:53,853 --> 00:42:55,071
is most likely the answer,

794
00:42:55,245 --> 00:42:57,378
and the least amount
of variables here

795
00:42:57,552 --> 00:42:59,902
is the agent from Ukraine.

796
00:43:00,076 --> 00:43:01,469
She hooked us.

797
00:43:01,730 --> 00:43:03,689
My guess is Yurimov is still
on the Russian front,

798
00:43:03,863 --> 00:43:05,560
and we're sitting on some actor

799
00:43:05,734 --> 00:43:08,041
from the fucking
Mossovet Theatre.

800
00:43:11,131 --> 00:43:12,654
Sorry.

801
00:43:12,915 --> 00:43:15,788
It's been a very long day,
a very long week.

802
00:43:16,049 --> 00:43:17,833
- I haven't slept, so--
- Oh, you're fine.

